+---
+id: PLAN-012-vtt-session-export
+status: draft
+date: 2026-11-05
+review_count: 0
+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: On-demand WebVTT export of session transcripts
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-006: the canonical session bundle is `<stem>.md` + `<stem>.srt` +
+  `<stem>.wav`, all plain local files readable with any tool. This plan
+  adds NO new stored artifact: the `.vtt` is a derived, on-demand export
+  of the canonical `.srt`, which remains the single source of truth.
+- ADR-007: pins the three-file layout, the bilingual cue format, and the
+  write semantics this export reads through (`stored.srt`). ADR-007
+  rejected WebVTT *as the canonical storage format*; an export view does
+  not revisit that decision. Persisting a `<stem>.vtt` sibling would
+  change the layout and require a new ADR first - out of scope here (see
+  Risks).
+- ADR-006: Fastify + TypeScript backend, React + TS + Tailwind web client;
+  no new dependencies (the SRT -> VTT conversion is written by hand, same
+  precedent as hand-rolled SRT emit/parse).
+- BDR-002: no new dependencies, no per-use cost; conversion is per-request
+  CPU over a < 100 KB file.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. `server/session/vtt.ts` (new): pure `srtToVtt` converter.
+2. `GET /api/sessions/:id/export.vtt` route returning the derived VTT as
+   a `text/vtt` attachment.
+3. `sessionsApi.vttUrl` in the web client plus a download affordance on
+   the Review page header and the Sessions list row.
+4. Tests for the converter and the route.
+
+Out of scope: writing `.vtt` to disk (would extend the ADR-007 bundle),
+editing stored `.srt`, WebVTT `<v Speaker>` voice tags, `NOTE` metadata
+blocks, any change to the live writer or socket protocol, SRT download
+button (the `.srt` already sits on disk next to the `.wav`).
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+### `server/session/vtt.ts`
+
+```ts
+export function srtToVtt(srt: string): string;
+```
+
+Transformation rules, applied block-by-block after splitting on `\n{2,}`
+and dropping empty blocks:
+
+- Output always starts with the literal line `WEBVTT`, then a blank line.
+- Per block: if the first line contains ` --> ` it is the timing line
+  (identifier-less cue); otherwise the first line is a cue identifier
+  kept verbatim on its own line (our SRT cue numbers become valid VTT
+  cue identifiers) and the second line is the timing line.
+- Timing line: emitted verbatim except every `,` replaced by `.`
+  (SRT `HH:MM:SS,mmm` -> VTT `HH:MM:SS.mmm`). No re-parsing or re-
+  formatting of the timestamps themselves.
+- Payload (text) lines: emitted verbatim except cue-text escaping, in
+  this order: `&` -> `&amp;`, then `<` -> `&lt;`, then `>` -> `&gt;`.
+  Escaping `>` also neutralizes a literal `-->` inside text (becomes
+  `--&gt;`), which raw VTT cue text forbids.
+- Blocks are joined by `\n\n`; the file ends with a single trailing
+  `\n` after the last block. Empty input yields `WEBVTT\n` exactly.
+
+Example. Stored `.srt` fragment:
+
+```
+1
+00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,800
+Speaker 1: Hello.
+Xin chào.
+```
+
+`srtToVtt` output:
+
+```
+WEBVTT
+
+1
+00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.800
+Speaker 1: Hello.
+Xin chào.
+```
+
+### HTTP route
+
+`GET /api/sessions/:id/export.vtt` in `registerSessionRoutes`:
+
+- `readSession(sessions.dir, id)`; `null` -> `404` with
+  `{ error: 'session not found: <id>' }` (same shape as the sibling
+  routes).
+- Otherwise `200` with headers:
+  - `Content-Type: text/vtt; charset=utf-8`
+  - `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="<stem>.vtt"` where
+    `stem` = `path.basename(stored.meta.file, '.md')`
+- Body: `srtToVtt(stored.srt)`. An empty transcript still returns `200`
+  with the `WEBVTT\n` body (a valid, importable empty file).
+- Works for in-progress sessions: the export reflects the `.srt` as it
+  exists at request time.
+
+### Web client
+
+```ts
+// web/src/lib/api.ts, inside sessionsApi:
+vttUrl: (id: string) =>
+  `/api/sessions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/export.vtt`,
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+1. `server/session/vtt.ts` (new): implement `srtToVtt` exactly per the
+   contract above. Pure function, no I/O, no imports needed beyond
+   nothing. Cue-text escaping helper `escapeVttText(line)` local to the
+   module.
+2. `server/session/vtt.test.ts` (new): see Test plan.
+3. `server/session/routes.ts`: register
+   `app.get('/api/sessions/:id/export.vtt', ...)` next to the existing
+   `:id` routes, importing `srtToVtt` and `node:path`. Fastify matches
+   the static `export.vtt` segment before the `:id` param route, so no
+   ordering hazard; still declare it after `GET /api/sessions/:id` for
+   readability.
+4. `server/app.test.ts`: add export-route cases (see Test plan) using the
+   same session-fixture harness the stored-session tests already use.
+5. `web/src/lib/api.ts`: add `vttUrl` per contract.
+6. `web/src/pages/Review.tsx`: in the header row (the
+   `flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2` div, after the speaker badges),
+   add a download button using Base UI's `render` prop (precedent:
+   `web/src/components/ui/alert-dialog.tsx`):
+
+   ```tsx
+   <Button
+     variant="outline"
+     size="sm"
+     render={<a href={sessionsApi.vttUrl(meta.id)} download />}
+   >
+     <Download data-icon="inline-start" />
+     VTT
+   </Button>
+   ```
+
+   `Download` joins the existing `lucide-react` import.
+7. `web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx`: in the row actions cell (next to the
+   Review button) add an icon-sized variant of the same link:
+   `size="icon-sm"`, `aria-label="Export VTT"`, `Download` icon only, no
+   text. Same `render={<a .../>}` pattern.
+8. Verify: `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm --prefix web run lint`.
+9. Commit, then log via `CONTEXTS/04-logs/event.py` (type `Feature`).
+
+## Test plan
+
+- `vtt.test.ts`:
+  - single bilingual cue -> `WEBVTT` header + identifier + dot-decimal
+    timing + both text lines;
+  - multi-cue input -> blocks separated by one blank line, file ends
+    with one `\n`;
+  - identifier-less block (first line is the timing line) -> no phantom
+    identifier emitted;
+  - escaping: text containing `a & b`, `<tag>`, `x --> y` produces
+    `a &amp; b`, `&lt;tag&gt;`, `x --&gt; y`;
+  - empty string and whitespace-only input -> `WEBVTT\n`;
+  - timestamp regression: `00:00:02,000` -> `00:00:02.000` (and an
+    hours-padded `01:02:03,456` case).
+- `app.test.ts`:
+  - `GET /api/sessions/:id/export.vtt` on a fixture session: `200`,
+    `content-type` starts with `text/vtt`, `content-disposition`
+    contains `filename="<stem>.vtt"`, body starts `WEBVTT` and contains
+    ` --> ` with `.` decimals;
+  - unknown id -> `404` with the standard error shape.
+- Manual acceptance: export from the Review button, drop the `.vtt`
+  next to the session `.wav` in VLC (or a video editor), confirm cues
+  render at the right times with speaker prefixes intact.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption (no clarification round per request): "vtt export" means a
+  downloadable `.vtt` derived on demand, not a fourth stored bundle
+  file. If the owner actually wants `<stem>.vtt` persisted in
+  `sessions/`, that extends the ADR-007 file layout and must be
+  escalated as a new ADR before implementation; the endpoint design
+  here stays valid either way.
+- Assumption: speaker identity exports as the existing `Name: ` text
+  prefix (byte-faithful to the SRT). `<v Name>` voice tags are a trivial
+  follow-up inside `srtToVtt` if wanted.
+- Escaping means exported text differs byte-wise from the `.srt` when
+  `&`, `<`, `>` occur; that is required for spec-valid VTT cue text.
+- `meta.file` is an absolute server path; only its basename reaches the
+  `Content-Disposition` header, so no server path leaks.
+- Cue identifiers (SRT numbers) survive as VTT cue identifiers; both
+  are `index + 1`, keeping the same binding to zero-based event indices
+  documented in ADR-007.
+- Exporting mid-session yields a VTT with EN-only cues where
+  translations have not landed yet - same transient state the `.srt`
+  itself exposes (ADR-007 consequence).
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `srtToVtt` implemented per contract; `vtt.test.ts` green.
+- [ ] `GET /api/sessions/:id/export.vtt` returns spec-valid VTT with
+      correct headers; `app.test.ts` green.
+- [ ] Review header and Sessions row expose the VTT download.
+- [ ] `npm run typecheck` clean; `npm test` green;
+      `npm --prefix web run lint` clean.
+- [ ] Manual: exported `.vtt` plays alongside the `.wav` in VLC or a
+      video editor with correct cue timing.
+- [ ] Plan status set to `implemented`; completion event logged.
-- 
